      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=133",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Liobagrus formosanus Regan, 1908</li><li>Common name: Formosan Bullhead</li><li>Type locality: Lake Candidius, Taiwan</li><li>Synonym: Liobagrus nantoensis</li><li>Identification: distinguished from congeners in having 5 branched dorsal-fin rays</li><li>IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=133",
      "html": "<p>Asia: endemic to Taiwan.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=133",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.6–7.6</li><li>Temperature: 12–20°C</li><li>Needs strong current.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=133",
      "html": "<p>Provide plenty of rocks as hiding places.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=133",
      "html": "<p>Feeds on small invertebrates in the wild. May adapt to prepared foods in aquaria.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=133",
      "html": "<p>Can be kept with other fishes in a temperate hillstream biotope. This typically includes loaches (e.g. Sinogastromyzon) and fast-water cyprinids (e.g. Barilius).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=133",
      "html": "<p>Not reported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=133",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: from the Greek leios, meaning smooth, and bagrus, a name usually used for catfishes, in reference to the smooth head. The specific epithet comes from Formosa, the former name of the island of Taiwan.</p>"
    },
